        <mxCell id="col1_9" value="<b>1. DATA SOURCES</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>Multi-Source Observational &amp; Reference Inputs</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#F0F9FF;strokeColor=#BAE6FD;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="155" width="330" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="src1_10" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;REAL-TIME TELEMETRY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;AWS Telemetry Network&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• 1,950+ Global stations &amp;amp; 296 Indian AWS
• IMD, WeatherUnion &amp;amp; Regional Mesonets
• 10-minute cadence surface observations
• Sensors: PRT Temp, Hygrometer, Barometer, Anemometer&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7DD3FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="220" width="290" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="src2_11" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;MODEL REFERENCE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Open-Meteo NWP Reference&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Numerical Weather Prediction model output
• Hourly baseline for global coordinates
• Reference temperature, wind, pressure
• Explicitly labeled NWP_MODEL_REFERENCE&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7DD3FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="385" width="290" height="135" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="src3_12" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0369A1;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;STANDARDS &amp;amp; LIMITS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Climatological Baselines&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• WMO-No. 8 physical atmospheric bounds
• Regional extreme temperature bounds (-45°C to +50°C)
• Standard sea-level pressure (1013.25 hPa)
• Barometric lapse rate constants (0.0065 K/m)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7DD3FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="545" width="290" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="src4_13" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;IN-SITU REPO DATA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Indian AWS Curated Dataset&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• High-density urban &amp;amp; rural stations
• Bengaluru (RR Nagar, Whitefield, Peenya)
• Delhi NCR, Mumbai, Chennai, Pune
• High-frequency localized microclimates&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7DD3FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="710" width="290" height="135" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="src5_14" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;IoT INTEGRATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;External Telemetry Streams&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• WeeWX weather station driver streams
• WOW-BE (Weather Observations Website)
• Weather Underground API format payloads&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7DD3FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="870" width="290" height="105" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="col2_15" value="<b>2. INGESTION &amp; DATA QUALITY</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>Normalization, Provenance &amp; Quality Labeling</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#334155;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="410" y="155" width="340" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ing1_16" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#475569;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;INGESTION ADAPTER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Multi-Protocol Ingestion Adapter&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Normalizes WeeWX, WOW-BE &amp;amp; Native JSON
• Unit conversion: °F → °C, inHg → hPa, mph → km/h
• Strict Pydantic schema validation
• Ingestion endpoint: POST /api/ingest&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="430" y="220" width="300" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ing2_17" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#475569;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;QUALITY LABELING&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Data Quality Guard &amp;amp; Labeler&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Zero-Pressure Policy: &amp;lt; 1 hPa treated as MISSING
• Zero-Temp check: valid 0°C vs absent data
• Channels labeled: VALID, MISSING, ZERO_SUBSTITUTED, INVALID, OUT_OF_RANGE
• Null-preservation: Never substitutes 0 for missing&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="430" y="385" width="300" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ing3_18" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#475569;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;PROVENANCE AUDITING&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Provenance &amp;amp; Freshness Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Source tagging: AWS_IN_SITU vs NWP_REFERENCE
• Freshness evaluation from real observation time
• Status classification: LIVE, STALE, UNKNOWN
• Safeguard: Rejects future timestamps&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="430" y="560" width="300" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ing4_19" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#475569;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;IN-MEMORY REGISTRY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Station Registry &amp;amp; Cache&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• In-memory indexed registry for 1,950+ stations
• Spatial indexing by lat/lon bounding box
• 24-hour observation history buffers
• Micro-caching with TTL invalidation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="430" y="725" width="300" height="135" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="col3_20" value="<b>3. PREPROCESSING &amp; FEATURES</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>Thermodynamic &amp; Kinematic Feature Pipelines</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#334155;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="780" y="155" width="350" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="proc1_21" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0F766E;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;HYPSOMETRIC REDUCTION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Barometric &amp;amp; Altitude Reduction&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Hypsometric barometric reduction to Sea-Level (MSL)
• SLP = P · (1 - 0.0065 · h / 288.15)^(-5.255)
• Elevation compensation for cross-station comparisons
• Detects station installation altitude errors&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="800" y="220" width="310" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="proc2_22" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0F766E;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;PSYCHROMETRICS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Psychrometric State Computation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Magnus-Tetens saturation vapor pressure e_s(T)
• Dew point derivation T_dew from (T, RH)
• Wet-bulb temperature approximation T_wb
• Vapor pressure deficit (VPD) feature calculation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="800" y="390" width="310" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="proc3_23" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0F766E;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;KINEMATIC DERIVATIVES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Temporal Kinematics Pipeline&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• 1st numerical derivative: Δx / Δt rate-of-change
• 2nd derivative: rate of acceleration d²x / dt²
• 72-sample rolling statistics (μ_24h, σ_24h)
• Interquartile range (IQR) &amp;amp; rolling z-scores&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="800" y="560" width="310" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="proc4_24" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0F766E;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;SPATIAL KD-TREE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Spatial KD-Tree Neighbor Search&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Haversine distance matrix for AWS clusters
• Dynamic k-nearest neighbors selection (d ≤ 50-250km)
• Elevation difference tracking Δh for lapse adjustment
• Minimum neighbor threshold enforcement (n ≥ 2)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="800" y="730" width="310" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="col4_25" value="<b>4. ATHER INTELLIGENCE ENGINE</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>5-Layer Concurrent Diagnostic &amp; Anomaly Detection Models</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#F0FDF4;strokeColor=#86EFAC;strokeWidth=2.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#15803D;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1160" y="155" width="740" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l1_26" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;LAYER 1 — THERMODYNAMIC INVARIANTS &amp;amp; VETO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Layer 1: Physics Validation Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Absolute thermodynamic limits (WMO-No. 8 standards)
• Temperature operating bounds: [-45°C, +50°C]
• Barometric limits: [920 hPa, 1065 hPa], RH: [0%, 100%]
• Clausius-Clapeyron: Dew point cannot exceed Dry bulb (T_dew ≤ T)
• Wet-bulb survivability threshold: T_wb ≤ 35°C
• Deterministic Physics VETO (Score = 1.0, bypasses statistical smoothing)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0284C7;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1185" y="220" width="690" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l2_27" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#4F46E5;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;LAYER 2 — KINEMATICS &amp;amp; FROZEN SENSOR DETECTOR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#3730A3;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Layer 2: Temporal Dynamics Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Diurnal step limits across 10-min interval: |ΔT| ≤ 3.5°C, |ΔP| ≤ 2.5 hPa, |ΔRH| ≤ 15%
• Instantaneous sensor jump detection (high 1st &amp;amp; 2nd derivatives)
• Frozen Sensor / Flatline Monitor: Var(X_12_readings) &amp;lt; 1e-6 (2h stuck values)
• Multi-scale rolling z-scores against diurnal baseline (threshold Z ≥ 3.5)
• Catches transmission glitches, ADC converter lockups, and electrical spikes&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#4F46E5;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#3730A3;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1185" y="380" width="690" height="135" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l3_28" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#7C3AED;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;LAYER 3 — CROSS-SENSOR PSYCHROMETRIC COUPLING&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#5B21B6;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Layer 3: Multivariate Consistency Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Psychrometric cross-channel coupling validation
• Temperature surge must correlate with Relative Humidity drop: Cov(T, RH) &amp;lt; 0
• Wind gust to sustained speed ratio: v_gust ≥ v_sustained
• Detects uncoupled failures (e.g. 100% RH at 38°C with crashing pressure)
• Identifies broken hygrometer polymer films &amp;amp; mismatched sensor pairs&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7C3AED;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#5B21B6;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1185" y="535" width="690" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l4_29" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#D97706;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;LAYER 4 — ELEVATION-CORRECTED SPATIAL KRIGING&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#B45309;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Layer 4: Spatial Consensus Engine (False-Alarm Killer)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Elevation-corrected Inverse Distance Weighting (IDW) Gaussian Kriging
• Local Z-score calculated against k-nearest active AWS (d ≤ 50-250 km)
• Expected value: T_consensus = Σ (w_i · (T_i - Γ·Δh)) / Σ w_i
• Disambiguates True Extreme Weather vs Sensor Malfunction:
  - Heatwave/Microburst: Station &amp;amp; Neighbors ALL elevate (Spatial Score = LOW)
  - Sensor Glitch: Target elevates in isolation while neighbors stay normal (Spatial Score = HIGH)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D97706;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#B45309;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1185" y="685" width="690" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l5_30" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#059669;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;LAYER 5 — CUSUM DRIFT &amp;amp; HEALTH INDEX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#065F46;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Layer 5: Sensor Health &amp;amp; Degradation Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Cumulative Sum (CUSUM) residual control charts on running residuals
• Non-parametric Mann-Kendall monotonic trend test on calibration offset
• Detects insidious slow drift (+0.2°C/week) undetectable by threshold checks
• Calculates Sensor Health Index [0-100%] &amp;amp; Estimated Days to Failure
• Flags aspirator fan dirt buildup, photodiode aging, hygrometer drift&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#065F46;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1185" y="845" width="690" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="col5_31" value="<b>5. CONFORMAL EVIDENCE FUSION</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>Multi-Evidence Uncertainty &amp; P-Value Calibration</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#FAF5FF;strokeColor=#E9D5FF;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#7E22CE;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1930" y="155" width="360" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fus1_32" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#7E22CE;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;COMPOSITE AGGREGATOR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#581C87;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Non-Conformity Aggregator&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Composite score: S = Σ (w_i · Score_i) / Σ w_i
• Physics: 0.35 | Temporal: 0.25 | Multi: 0.20
• Spatial: 0.15 | Drift: 0.05
• Acute layer trigger checks (Score_i ≥ 0.70-0.80)
• Physics VETO priority bypass (deterministic 0.95)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C084FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#581C87;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1950" y="220" width="320" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fus2_33" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#7E22CE;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;CONFORMAL CALIBRATOR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#581C87;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Empirical Conformal Calibrator&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Calibrated non-conformity threshold quantile
• Target false-alarm rate: α = 0.001 (MAPIE standard)
• Empirical p-value computation against clean set
• Rigorous statistical bounds for field escalation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C084FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#581C87;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1950" y="395" width="320" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fus3_34" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#7E22CE;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;CALIBRATED CONFIDENCE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#581C87;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Evidence-Quality Confidence Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Dynamic confidence [0.10 - 0.97] without artificial floors
• Scaled by Layer Coverage Ratio (valid channel fraction)
• Scaled by Layer Agreement Factor (low inter-layer variance)
• Scarcity Penalties: spatial neighbor &amp;lt; 3, history &amp;lt; 5
• Single-layer evidence strictly capped at 0.65&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C084FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#581C87;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1950" y="570" width="320" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fus4_35" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#7E22CE;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;DECISION SYNTHESIZER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#581C87;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Severity &amp;amp; Status Synthesizer&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Severity Score: 0.6 · Peak_Layer + 0.4 · Nonconf_Score
• Three Canonical Anomaly Status States:
  🟢 NORMAL (Severity &amp;lt; 0.35, Peak &amp;lt; 0.60)
  🟡 WARNING (Severity ≥ 0.35 or low confidence)
  🔴 ANOMALY (Severity ≥ 0.60 &amp;amp; Confidence ≥ 0.30)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C084FC;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#581C87;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1950" y="755" width="320" height="165" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="col6_36" value="<b>6. ROOT-CAUSE &amp; SELF-HEALING</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>Diagnostic Disambiguation &amp; Telemetry Imputation</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#FFFBEB;strokeColor=#FDE68A;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#B45309;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2320" y="155" width="400" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rc1_37" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#D97706;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;FAULT CLASSIFICATION HIERARCHY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#92400E;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Hierarchical Root Cause Classifier&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Disambiguates 10 confirmed FaultType categories:
  1. SENSOR_SPIKE (Temporal High + Spatial High)
  2. FROZEN_SENSOR (Zero variance across 2h window)
  3. CALIBRATION_DRIFT (Persistent CUSUM accumulation)
  4. SINGLE_CHANNEL_FAULT (Isolated physical anomaly)
  5. GENUINE_EXTREME_WEATHER (Spatial consensus corroboration)
  6. POSSIBLE_WEATHER_CHANGE (Moderate spatial confirmation)
  7. NOISE_BURST (Isolated statistical fluctuation)
  8. COMMUNICATION_OUTAGE (Missing telemetry)
  9. INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE (Weak cross-layer signal)
  10. MODEL_REFERENCE_INCONSISTENCY (NWP anomaly)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#F59E0B;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#92400E;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2340" y="220" width="360" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rc2_38" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#D97706;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;DIAGNOSTIC EXPLAINABILITY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#92400E;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Plain-English Explainability Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Formats structured diagnostic rationale
• Primary Signal culprit identification
• Ranked alternative hypotheses with confidence
• Specific Field Operator Recommended Actions
• e.g. &amp;#x27;Inspect thermistor radiation shield for debris&amp;#x27;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#F59E0B;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#92400E;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2340" y="480" width="360" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rc3_39" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#D97706;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;SELF-HEALING IMPUTATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#92400E;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Data Reconstruction / Self-Healing&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Synthesizes physically coherent replacement values
• Imputation Hierarchy:
  1. Priority 1: Spatial Neighbor Consensus IDW
  2. Priority 2: Thermodynamic Magnus-Tetens Inversion
  3. Priority 3: Temporal Autoregressive Smoothing
• Maintains Raw Observation + Imputed Corrected Value&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#F59E0B;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#92400E;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2340" y="650" width="360" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rc4_40" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#D97706;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;CANONICAL DIAGNOSIS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#92400E;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Canonical §16 Analysis Object&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Standardized payload for API &amp;amp; Frontend consumption
• Station metadata, observation provenance, freshness
• Overall score, threshold, layer breakdown &amp;amp; reasons
• Audit-ready structured incident snapshot&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#F59E0B;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#92400E;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2340" y="830" width="360" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="col7_41" value="<b>7. PERSISTENCE, API &amp; METEOROLOGICAL COMMAND CENTER</b><br><span style='font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;color:#475569;'>Storage State Machine, FastAPI Endpoints &amp; React 19 / MapLibre Operations</span>" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=40;rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=16;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2750" y="155" width="860" height="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="db_box_42" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#334155;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;INCIDENT STATE MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;SQLite WAL Persistence&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Operational Incidents Table (incidents.db)
• Incident Timeline Audit Trail
• State Machine Transitions:
  NEW → ACKNOWLEDGED → INVESTIGATING
  → ESCALATED → RESOLVED / DISMISSED
• Fingerprinting: (station_id, param, fault)
• Severity Mapping: CRITICAL (P1), WARNING (P2), INFO (P3/P4)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#64748B;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2770" y="220" width="260" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cache_box_43" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#334155;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;LOCAL DATASTORE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Station Datasets &amp;amp; Caches&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• data/stations.json: 1,950+ stations
• WeatherUnionInfra.csv (Indian AWS)
• data/station_history.json: 24h diurnal series
• .weather_cache.json: Open-Meteo cache
• Thread-safe sqlite3 WAL lock manager&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#64748B;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0F172A;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2770" y="450" width="260" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="api_box_44" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;REST API SERVICES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;FastAPI REST API Core&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• GET /api/health (Registry &amp;amp; system state)
• GET /api/stations (Viewport Bounding-Box GeoJSON)
• GET /api/stations/{id} (Full telemetry &amp;amp; sensors)
• GET /api/stations/{id}/anomaly (5-Layer scores)
• GET /api/stations/{id}/debug (End-to-end trace)
• POST /api/ingest (Multi-protocol ingest)
• GET/POST /api/incidents (Incident triage &amp;amp; state)
• GET /api/weather/grid (WebGL meteorological field)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0284C7;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3050" y="220" width="250" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="grid_box_45" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#0284C7;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;VANE GRID SERVICE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#0369A1;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Meteorological Field Engine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• Generates scalar 0.25° temperature grid
• Generates vector wind fields (U, V components)
• Real-time interpolation for MapLibre WebGL
• Dynamic Vane visualizer integration&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0284C7;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0369A1;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3050" y="480" width="250" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ui_map_46" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;margin-bottom:6px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;background-color:#4F46E5;color:#ffffff;font-size:10px;font-weight:bold;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;&#x27;&gt;MAPLIBRE GPU MAP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#3730A3;margin-bottom:4px;&#x27;&gt;Interactive 2D Weather Map&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#475569;line-height:1.35;&#x27;&gt;• MapLibre GL GPU-accelerated clustering
• 1,950+ Global &amp;amp; 296 Indian AWS at 60 FPS
• Dark Carto &amp;amp; Satellite Basemap switching
• Dynamic scalar heatmaps &amp;amp; vector wind particles
• Visual station status: Normal, Warning, Anomaly&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#4F46E5;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#3730A3;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;shadow=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3320" y="220" width="270" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
